/* High / Medium guidance script · p-cctv-everywhere (Advantages / disadvantages: "Do the advantages outweigh …?") · C1 tier, Band 7.0–8.0
   Built on the C1 Advantage playbook lines (template.js c1-advantage-intro, c1-advantage-bodyA, c1-advantage-bodyB,
   c1-advantage-conclusion; T.Chris's three levels, 15 Nov 2026), populated with the prompt's C1 variables (prompts-2.js vars.C1).
   The playbook lines read more naturally for an outweigh question than the C1 Standard and keep the frame share under 40%.
   Type Switch Card (ADVANTAGE): Facet A = the main advantage (deterrence and evidence), Nuance A = its limit (displacement),
   Facet B = the main disadvantage (privacy and normalised observation), Nuance B = how far it can be managed (retention and
   access rules), Position = which side outweighs, and on what condition. "Advantages" / "disadvantages" are plural: Body A adds
   the evidence advantage in a development sentence, Body B adds a second cost (a chilling effect on protest).
   The frame names each facet three times: short forms in the introduction and the conclusion, the full facet in the body.
   The Core Topic is reshaped to follow "The emergence of"; the other C1 variables are the bank's wording.
   Examples stay generic (no named city, no figure). Variable steps (v: …) that use the duel's near-misses have the duel's right
   answer. Standard: docs/GUIDE-AUTHORING-T2.md §12. Test: node tools/guide-test.js p-cctv-everywhere.c1 --essay */
